# checkpoint-links: every row makes real shadow-git snapshots and rewinds over its own link fixtures — measured standalone
# on 2026-10-30 (lane checkpoint-links): 66 s at review 6.2, 79 s at final review 2; with the undo-closure rows
# (fr3-fr6: a capped runner, 60 and 120 entry budgets) 308 s, 461 s and 477 s while other gates held the CPU at 100%,
# near the 600 s limit: splitting row 20 into a file of its own is the follow-up if a gate cuts it off. Undo review 1's
# rows went to test/checkpoint-undo.test.js instead, so this file did not grow: 324 s and 187 s at that fix, other gates
# running (the first at 100% CPU). At undo review 2's fix (2026-10-30/31, other gates running): 121 s and 123 s at about
# 45% CPU, 163 s and 196 s at about 90%. At undo review 3's fix (2026-10-31, no new rows here): 123 s and 126 s at
# 40-57% CPU. At undo review 4's fix (2026-10-31, no new rows here): 150 s at 94% CPU, and 447 s in a run near 100%.
# At undo review 5's fix (2026-10-31, no new rows here; each rewind now lists both trees' modes once): 219 s at 66% CPU.
# Undo review 6 measured 323 s at 81% CPU, one row at a time. Since its fix the rows run four at a time, each on its
# own agent, and no Git starts a console host (test/helpers/checkpoint-rows.js). Measured standalone through
# scripts/run-test-list.mjs on 2026-11-01, the box rebooted at 12:49 that day: 41 s at 61% CPU and 48 s at 83%
# beside another gate, 130 s at 100% beside another; 132 s at 99% and 128 s at 100% with busy threads added; 92 s at 100%
# with 16 game instances and no gate, 91 s at 100% with 12-16 of them and the run queue at 45-81. ab10c33's file, one row
# at a time, that day: 142 s at 61%. Before that reboot, the box up since 2026-10-30 18:37 and a lone
# `git --version` taking 0.2-3 s to start and end (19-30 ms after it, 90-180 ms at 100% CPU): 141 s at 64% (2026-11-01
# 00:24); with a console host beside every Git (2026-10-31), 337 s at 94% and 381 s at 88%, cut off at 600 s once at 97%.
# At undo review 7's fix (2026-11-01 evening, no new rows here): 54 s at 76% and 77 s at 93% beside two other gates, 115 s
# at 100% with busy threads added.
test/checkpoint-links.test.js
# checkpoint-undo: every row rewinds and undoes through real shadow-git, ten of them through the real runner capped at
# 1500 bytes, ten under a 40-80 entry walk budget, undo review 3's over clones, a linked worktree and `.git` junctions —
# measured standalone (lane checkpoint-links): 239 s before its W rows with other gates holding the CPU at 100%, 110 s
# with them, other gates running (undo review 1, 2026-10-30); with undo review 2's rows 90 s at about 45% CPU, 98 s and
# 152 s at about 90% (2026-10-30/31); with undo review 3's 121 s and 143 s at 40-57% CPU (2026-10-31); at undo review
# 4's fix 157 s at 74% CPU (its rows went to checkpoint-undo-gitlinks, below, which keeps both under 600 s); at undo
# review 5's, no new rows, 265 s at 77% (its 126 new Git calls, the modes each rewind lists, are 6% of its 2272); undo
# review 6 measured 471 s at 86%, one row at a time (79% of the 600 s cap). Since its fix the rows run four at a time,
# each on its own agent, and no Git starts a console host, measured as checkpoint-links was (2026-11-01, after the
# reboot): 35 s at 63% CPU and 50 s at 87% beside another gate, 95 s at 99% beside another; 127 s and 133 s at 100%
# with busy threads added; 127 s and 124 s at 100% with 12-16 game instances and no gate; ab10c33's file 162 s at 75%. Before that reboot: 155 s at 62% (2026-11-01 00:21); with a
# console host beside every Git (2026-10-31), 271 s at 71% and 331 s at 86%, cut off at 600 s once at 97%. At undo review
# 7's fix (2026-11-01 evening, no new rows here): 64 s at 78% and 66 s at 87% beside two other gates, 124 s at 100% with busy
# threads added.
# It runs on the FAST gate since undo review 2, beside checkpoint-links: the HTTP gate (57 min deadline) took
# 46m25s-55m26s in its ten runs of 2026-10-28 to -30 and ran out of time in three. The fast gate (47 min) took
# 24m01s-37m38s in its ten latest local runs without the lane, which leaves 9m22s after its slowest. The lane's three
# fast-gate steps together, 2026-11-01 after the reboot: 93 s at 54-63% CPU and 127 s at 83-88% beside another gate,
# 259 s at 96-100% beside another, 290 s at 92-100% and 318 s at 100% with busy threads added, 332 s at 99-100% with 16
# game instances and no gate, 457 s at 100% with 12-16 of them and the run queue at 45-81 (ab10c33's files 383 s at
# 61-75%); no quiet box that day. Before that reboot: 388 s at 62-70%, and undo review 6 measured ab10c33's 15m53s at 81-86%. CPU share alone
# does not say what these steps take: starting one Git held a file's main thread 43-114 ms before the reboot, 5-7 ms
# after it, even at 100%. At undo review 7's fix, with its rows in checkpoint-undo-gitlinks, that evening: 193 s and 219 s at
# 76-93% beside two other gates, 388 s at 100% with busy threads added, no step past 149 s, a quarter of its cap. No run has
# timed them on Linux, where the CI fast-gate job has 30-87 s of room under its 25 minutes; 15 of the new rows skip where
# the file system does not fold case.
test/checkpoint-undo.test.js
# checkpoint-undo-gitlinks: undo review 4's rows (lane checkpoint-links: a gitlink a rewind records over a FILE, the depth
# its undo lists to, Git's nesting answer asked again), undo review 5's (a symbolic link an older capture recorded, a
# FILE spelled in another case) and undo review 6's (a FILE no capture took where the shadow index still tracks paths
# below its name), each rewinding and undoing through real shadow-git, the depth rows under a 5-level walk, N2 and
# sym5 through the real runner capped at 1500 bytes. Split from checkpoint-undo, which they took to 413 s and 559 s
# with other gates holding the CPU at 77-100%, so each step keeps room under 600 s. Measured standalone on 2026-10-31,
# other gates running: 48 s at 79% CPU, and 48-120 s for the same rows while they were checked; with undo review 5's
# rows 115 s at 91% CPU and 212 s at 93%, and 159 s at 82% one row at a time at undo review 6. Since its fix the rows
# run four at a time and no Git starts a console host, measured as checkpoint-links was, with undo review 6's rows
# (2026-11-01, after the reboot): 17 s at 54% CPU and 29 s at 88% beside another gate, 34 s at 96% beside another; 31 s
# at 92% and 57 s at 100% with busy threads added; 113 s at 99% with 16 game instances and no gate, 242 s at 100% with
# 12-16 of them and the run queue at 45-81; ab10c33's file 79 s at 73%. Before that reboot: 92 s at 70%
# (2026-11-01 00:20); with a console host beside every Git (2026-10-31), 185 s at 70%, 189 s at 85% and 391 s at 96%.
# With undo review 7's rows (names Git and the file system read apart, the bytes, the person's Git config, a failed launch:
# 340 assertions against 151; 2026-11-01 evening): 73 s and 78 s at 87% beside two other gates, 149 s at 100% with busy threads
# added.
test/checkpoint-undo-gitlinks.test.js
